ationery front: envelopes <a href="https://www.mygeolopes.com/?gad_source=1&amp;gad_campaignid=23917136130&amp;gclid=Cj0KCQjw39zSBhDhARIsANammDtDZQk9kYOxNr_xRUU3PwuDKJ-5DWbrac5vj1PT4CvwN0XVFc0iIc8aAo1fEALw_wcB">made from old U.S. Geological Survey maps</a>! (From Jason Hillyer)</p></li><li><p>Nice, thoughtful review of a new book featuring <a href="https://www.digitalcameraworld.com/photography/books/ben-marcin-photographed-dozens-of-abandoned-houses-in-exactly-the-same-way-for-20-years-and-his-new-book-is-a-masterclass-in-editing">photos of abandoned houses</a> in and around Baltimore. (Another one from Jason Hillyer)</p></li><li><p>Size matters: The famous Oscar Mayer weinermobile <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reels/DbCXeLEtcoR/">got stuck in a tunnel</a>! (From Adriene Zepka)</p></li><li><p>Here&#8217;s a faaaascinating piece on the newest movie craze: <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/23/business/media/movie-theaters-popcorn-buckets.html?unlocked_article_code=1.z1A.bXCx.WbQvwU6HVSSo&amp;smid=url-share">collectible popcorn buckets</a>. That article is both informative and very entertainingly written &#8212; highly recommended!</p></li><li><p>It&#8217;s been so hot in Japan that they had to <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/23/weather/japan-excessive-heat-kokushobi.html?unlocked_article_code=1.0FA.dZtI.c3uQIZlMqW05&amp;smid=url-share">come up with a new word for it</a>.</p></li></ul><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.inconspicuous.info/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.inconspicuous.info/subscribe?"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!mWij!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.a