   ]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[A Very Special Postal Art Project]]></title><description><![CDATA[For 36 years, a man mailed letters to himself and matched his handwriting on the envelopes to the visual themes of the stamps, with amazing results.]]></description><link>https://www.inconspicuous.info/p/a-very-special-postal-art-project</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.inconspicuous.info/p/a-very-special-postal-art-project</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Paul Lukas]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 16 Jun 2026 18:00:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_2400,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg" width="1200" height="651.9230769230769" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:false,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;large&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:791,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:1200,&quot;bytes&quot;:221504,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.inconspicuous.info/i/201987823?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:&quot;center&quot;,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-large" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!rvJR!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F499073ec-0460-415e-b26a-1e7bd083e10e_1600x869.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><em>(Photo via San Francisco History Center)</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>Last month I wrote about a <a href="https://www.inconspicuous.info/p/a-very-special-utterly-enjoyable">great piece of mail</a> that I received from an IC reader. That prompted a comment from another reader, named Matt Douma, who wrote:</p><blockquote><p>[This] reminds me of a show I saw at the San Francisco Public Library years ago of postcards and letters that a stamp collector mailed to himself, with his name and address hand-lettered to reflect the design of the stamps. I stumbled across it by accident, and it was one of the best displays of art I've ever seen. I highly recommend <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&amp;v=3huCgp12MEc&amp;sttick=0">this video</a> about the project.</p></blockquote><p>The video is about 10 minutes long, and it took me a few days before I got around to watching it. But once I did, I was completely blown away, just as Matt was. After digging a bit deeper and learning more, I&#8217;m not so sure I&#8217;d go so far as to call it one of the best displays of art I&#8217;ve ever seen, but it&#8217;s definitely one of the best <em>long-term art projects</em> I&#8217;ve ever seen.</p><p>Here&#8217;s the story: In 1968, a guy in San Francisco named Alan Blackman began mailing letters to himself, a habit he maintained for 36 years. These were all <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_day_of_issue">first-day covers</a>, meaning that he mailed the letters using stamps that had just been released that day, so the stamps received a special &#8220;First Day of Issue&#8221; cancellation mark. (More on this in a minute.) Blackman was a calligrapher, and at some point he began matching the lettering style of his name and address on the envelopes to the visual style and/or thematic content of the stamps. For example, when a new Uncle Sam stamp was issued in 1998, Blackman styled his address like a flag-themed top hat (as seen in the photo at the top of this page).</p><p>Sometimes Blackman&#8217;s lettering designs depicted figures or characters, as in the case of the address accompanying these 1997 Bug Bunny stamps:</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!jPnw!,f_auto