   ]]></content:encoded></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can You Design a New Inconspicuous Consumption T-Shirt?]]></title><description><![CDATA[If so, then I have a project for you. Plus a new Inconspicuous News Roundup!]]></description><link>https://www.inconspicuous.info/p/can-you-design-a-new-inconspicuous</link><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.inconspicuous.info/p/can-you-design-a-new-inconspicuous</guid><dc:creator><![CDATA[Paul Lukas]]></dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jun 2026 13:25:37 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/fc07b5ce-f9e0-49d6-a1fe-d148099e87cc_2223x1277.jpeg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/><content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><em><strong>Note: </strong>This post is not paywalled. Enjoy!</em></p><div><hr></div><p>Lately I&#8217;ve been thinking a bit about Inconspicuous Consumption&#8217;s shorthand abbreviation &#8212; IC. If you say it out loud, it sounds like &#8220;I see.&#8221; That feels right, because Inconspicuous Consumption is often about seeing small details, seeing things that other people miss, the surprise of discovery, and so on. You see? IC!</p><p>I&#8217;ve been thinking that the resonance between &#8220;IC&#8221; and &#8220;I see&#8221; might make the basis for a good logo or T-shirt. For a while I tinkered with a lowercase &#8220;i&#8221; dotted with an eyeball, like this:</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2IXB!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2abfabc4-f54a-4b8e-83ff-29ee108ce6b3_2934x1719.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2IXB!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2abfabc4-f54a-4b8e-83ff-2