lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><em>(Image from Reddit user secretarydesk)</em></figcaption></figure></div><ul><li><p>You know how the USPS logo shows a stylized eagle? A bird-centric artist named Alex Tominson has reimagined the logo for all of the country&#8217;s official state birds (see above).</p></li><li><p>Did you know that Nepal has its own time zone, which is 15 minutes off from all the others? <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/27/world/asia/nepal-time-15-minutes.html?unlocked_article_code=1.llA.l7_d.pX2iggRqVHxr&amp;smid=url-share">It&#8217;s true</a>!</p></li><li><p>Oh man, check out this absolutely sensational pop-up book &#8212; so good (from Trish Clark):</p></li></ul><div id="youtube2-zaKhzIsqlrE" class="youtube-wrap" data-attrs="{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;zaKhzIsqlrE&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:null,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}" data-component-name="Youtube2ToDOM"><div class="youtube-inner"><iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/zaKhzIsqlrE?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0" frameborder="0" loading="lazy" gesture="media" allow="autoplay; fullscreen" allowautoplay="true" allowfullscreen="true" width="728" height="409"></iframe></div></div><ul><li><p>Miriam Sicherman spotted this car with a 1976 Carter/Mondale bumper sticker (see below). Not sure if that&#8217;s just an isolated instance or if retro political bumper stickers are a trend. Anyone know more?</p></li></ul><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!gNHI!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F08d99867-53c1-44cb-9857-04c3b5c424ca_1536x2048.jpeg