2w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!PF2Z!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F188ad3d0-aa1d-450f-b828-567ef9d68974_1966x1194.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw" fetchpriority="high"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><em>This wrapper has had quite an unusual existence. (Photo by Paul)</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>In 1996 &#8212; that&#8217;s 30 years ago &#8212; my friends Eve and David were doing some renovations on their home in Portland, Oregon. At one point they pulled up a floorboard and saw an old Juicy Fruit gum wrapper that had somehow ended up there, probably after being discarded by a worker. It looked very much like the brand&#8217;s then-current wrapper design, except for the slogan printed beneath the Juicy Fruit logo: &#8220;The Gum With the Fascinating Artificial Flavor.&#8221;</p><p>They don&#8217;t write marketing pitches like that anymore! Eve and David knew this was precisely the type of thing I tend to be intrigued by, so they mailed the wrapper to me. I ended up writing about it in 1997, as part of a magazine article about products with unusual flavors, and then the following year I reprinted that article in issue No. 8 of my zine, <em>Beer Frame: The Journal of Inconspicuous Consumption</em>.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg" width="1456" height="1218" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1218,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:3089708,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.inconspicuous.info/i/196217981?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!eCuY!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3b5a588-463f-4137-be5e-f74a30780545_3207x2683.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><em>A two-page spread from issue No. 8 of </em>Beer Frame<em>, published in March 1998, showing part of an article about unusual flavors. The Juicy Fruit wrapper at upper-left is the same one shown at the beginning of this Substack article. (Photo by Paul)</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>After I wrote about the wrapper, I put it in a drawer where I typically save little oddball treasures. And then &#8230; honestly, I&#8217;m not sure what happened after that. Although I don&#8217;t recall the exact timeline, I know at some point I realized that the Juicy Fruit wrapper had disappeared. Had I carelessly discarded it? Was it hidden away in a spot where I hadn&#8217;t thought to look for it? Did it somehow get separated from the rest of my possessions during a move? All I knew for sure was that I felt shitty about losing this special gift that two friends had sent to me.</p>
