encraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class="image-caption"><em>(Photo by Paul)</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>I was walking down Canal Street in Manhattan the other day with my friend (and IC reader!) Adriene Zepka when I noticed the Drake&#8217;s sign shown above and stopped to take a photo of it. &#8220;Wait, you&#8217;re photographing <em>that</em>?&#8221; she said. &#8220;What&#8217;s so special about it?&#8221;</p><p>The answer, of course, is that the Drake&#8217;s sign presents one possible answer to an eternal typographic question: Where should the apostrophe be positioned on a vertically lettered sign for a business with a possessive name?</p><p>There&#8217;s no straightforward solution to this conundrum, but there are four primary approaches that signmakers have taken over the years, plus a workaround option, each of which feels at least somewhat imperfect. Let&#8217;s take a look at each one, beginning with&#8230;</p><h3>1. Put the Apostrophe in Front of the &#8220;S&#8221;</h3><p>The Drake&#8217;s sign on falls into this category. Based on my photo research, however, this is a relatively uncommon option, with only a few other examples that I could find:</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg 1456w" sizes="100vw"><img src="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2jL6!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fd8090a8b-50b9-4a5d-be80-89887e9f2387_4608x3456.jpeg" width="1456" height="1092"